{"id":"mahabharata-12-003","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":3,"title":"तृतीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 3 · Karna and Parashurama","summary":{"en":"Parashurama is pleased with Karna's devotion and teaches him the weapon, and one day sleeps with his head on Karna's lap. A worm bores into Karna's thigh and he bears the pain in silence, which reveals that he is not a brahmin.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣನ ಭಕ್ತಿಗೆ ಪರಶುರಾಮ ಸಂತೋಷಗೊಂಡು ಅಸ್ತ್ರ ಕಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಒಂದು ದಿನ ಕರ್ಣನ ತೊಡೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ತಲೆಯಿಟ್ಟು ಮಲಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹುಳು ಕರ್ಣನ ತೊಡೆ ಕೊರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ; ನೋವನ್ನು ಮೌನವಾಗಿ ಸಹಿಸುವುದು ಅವನು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"परशुराम कर्ण की भक्ति से प्रसन्न होकर उसे अस्त्र सिखाते हैं और एक दिन उसकी जंघा पर सिर रखकर सोते हैं। एक कीड़ा कर्ण की जंघा को छेदता है और वह पीड़ा मौन सहता है, जिससे प्रकट होता है कि वह ब्राह्मण नहीं है।","te":"కర్ణుని భక్తికి పరశురాముడు సంతోషించి అస్త్రం నేర్పి ఒక రోజు కర్ణుని తొడపై తల పెట్టి నిద్రిస్తాడు. ఒక పురుగు కర్ణుని తొడను తొలుస్తుంది; నొప్పిని మౌనంగా భరించడం అతడు బ్రాహ్మణుడు కాదని తెలియజేస్తుంది.","ta":"கர்ணனின் பக்தியால் மகிழ்ந்த பரசுராமர் அவனுக்கு அஸ்திரம் கற்பித்து, ஒருநாள் அவன் மடியில் தலைவைத்து உறங்குகிறார். ஒரு புழு கர்ணனின் தொடையைத் துளைக்க, வலியை அவன் மௌனமாகத் தாங்குவது அவன் அந்தணன் அல்லன் எனக் காட்டுகிறது.","ml":"പരശുരാമൻ കർണ്ണന്റെ ഭക്തിയിൽ സന്തുഷ്ടനായി അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് ആയുധവിദ്യ പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ഒരു ദിവസം അദ്ദേഹം കർണ്ണന്റെ മടിയിൽ തല വെച്ച് ഉറങ്ങുന്നു. ഒരു പുഴു കർണ്ണന്റെ തുടയിൽ തുളച്ചുകയറുന്നു; വേദന നിശ്ശബ്ദം സഹിക്കുന്നതിലൂടെ അദ്ദേഹം ബ്രാഹ്മണനല്ലെന്ന് വെളിപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.3; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कर्णस्य बाहुवीर्येण प्रश्रयेण दमेन च ।\nतुतोष भृगुशार्दूलो गुरुशुश्रूषया तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tiger among the Bhrigus was pleased with Karna's strength of arm, his humility, his self-control, and his service to his teacher."}},{"n":2,"text":"तस्मै स विधिवत्कृत्स्नं ब्रह्मास्त्रं सनिवर्तनम् ।\nप्रोवाचाखिलमव्यग्रं तपस्वी सुतपस्विने ॥","meaning":{"en":"That ascetic then patiently taught the ascetic Karna the entire Brahma weapon, with its recall, as the rule requires."}},{"n":3,"text":"विदितास्त्रस्ततः कर्णो रममाणोऽऽश्रमे भृगोः ।\nचकार वै धनुर्वेदे यत्नमद्भुतविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having learned the weapon, Karna of wondrous prowess lived happily in Bhrigu's hermitage and devoted himself to archery."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः कदाचिद्रामस्तु चरन्नाश्रममन्तिकात् ।\nकर्णेन सहितो धीमानुपवासेन कर्शितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one day Rama, wise and weakened by fasting, was walking near the hermitage with Karna."}},{"n":5,"text":"सुष्वाप जामदग्न्यो वै विस्रम्भोत्पन्नसौहृदः ।\nकर्णस्योत्सङ्ग आधाय शिरः क्लान्तमना गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jamadagni's son, who had grown fond of Karna out of trust, lay down to sleep, resting his head, with tired mind, on Karna's lap."}},{"n":6,"text":"अथ कृमिः श्लेष्ममयो मांसशोणितभोजनः ।\nदारुणो दारुणस्पर्शः कर्णस्याभ्याशमागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a worm, born of phlegm, living on flesh and blood, fierce and cruel to the touch, came close to Karna."}},{"n":7,"text":"स तस्योरुमथासाद्य बिभेद रुधिराशनः ।\nन चैनमशकत्क्षेप्तुं हन्तुं वापि गुरोर्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Settling on his thigh, that blood-drinker bored into it. Karna could neither throw it off nor kill it, for fear of his teacher."}},{"n":8,"text":"संदश्यमानोऽपि तथा कृमिणा तेन भारत ।\nगुरुप्रबोधशङ्की च तमुपैक्षत सूतजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the worm was biting him so, Bharata, the charioteer's son, afraid of waking his teacher, ignored it."}},{"n":9,"text":"कर्णस्तु वेदनां धैर्यादसह्यां विनिगृह्य ताम् ।\nअकम्पन्नव्यथंश्चैव धारयामास भार्गवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna firmly held down the unbearable pain with fortitude, and without trembling or flinching he kept supporting the Bhargava."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदा तु रुधिरेणाङ्गे परिस्पृष्टो भृगूद्वहः ।\nतदाबुध्यत तेजस्वी संतप्तश्चेदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But when the Bhrigu hero was touched by blood on his body, the radiant sage woke, and in distress he said this."}},{"n":11,"text":"अहोऽस्म्यशुचितां प्राप्तः किमिदं क्रियते त्वया ।\nकथयस्व भयं त्यक्त्वा याथातथ्यमिदं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Alas, I have been made unclean! What are you doing? Tell me the truth of this without fear.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"तस्य कर्णस्तदाचष्ट कृमिणा परिभक्षणम् ।\nददर्श रामस्तं चापि कृमिं सूकरसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna then told him that a worm had been eating him, and Rama saw that worm, which was like a boar."}},{"n":13,"text":"अष्टपादं तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रं सूचीभिरिव संवृतम् ।\nरोमभिः संनिरुद्धाङ्गमलर्कं नाम नामतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It had eight feet and sharp tusks, and its body was covered with bristles like needles. Its name was Alarka."}},{"n":14,"text":"स दृष्टमात्रो रामेण कृमिः प्राणानवासृजत् ।\nतस्मिन्नेवासृक्संक्लिन्ने तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The moment Rama saw it, the worm gave up its life; and with the blood still wet on it, a marvel took place."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षे ददृशे विश्वरूपः करालवान् ।\nराक्षसो लोहितग्रीवः कृष्णाङ्गो मेघवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the sky appeared a fearsome being of many shapes, a rakshasa with red neck and black limbs, riding a cloud."}},{"n":16,"text":"स रामं प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा बभाषे पूर्णमानसः ।\nस्वस्ति ते भृगुशार्दूल गमिष्यामि यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With joined palms and a glad heart he said to Rama: \"Blessings on you, tiger of the Bhrigus. I shall go back the way I came."}},{"n":17,"text":"मोक्षितो नरकादस्मि भवता मुनिसत्तम ।\nभद्रं च तेऽस्तु नन्दिश्च प्रियं मे भवता कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, best of sages, have freed me from hell. May good come to you and joy. You have done what I most wished.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"तमुवाच महाबाहुर्जामदग्न्यः प्रतापवान् ।\nकस्त्वं कस्माच्च नरकं प्रतिपन्नो ब्रवीहि तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed, glorious Jamadagni's son said to him: \"Who are you, and why did you fall into hell? Tell me.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"सोऽब्रवीदहमासं प्राग्गृत्सो नाम महासुरः ।\nपुरा देवयुगे तात भृगोस्तुल्यवया इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: \"Long ago, in the age of the gods, I was a great asura named Gritsa, about the same age as Bhrigu, dear one."}},{"n":20,"text":"सोऽहं भृगोः सुदयितां भार्यामपहरं बलात् ।\nमहर्षेरभिशापेन कृमिभूतोऽपतं भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I forcibly carried off the beloved wife of Bhrigu, and by the great sage's curse I fell to earth as a worm."}},{"n":21,"text":"अब्रवीत्तु स मां क्रोधात्तव पूर्वपितामहः ।\nमूत्रश्लेष्माशनः पाप निरयं प्रतिपत्स्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger your forefather said to me: 'Sinner, you will go to a hell where you will eat urine and phlegm.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"शापस्यान्तो भवेद्ब्रह्मन्नित्येवं तमथाब्रुवम् ।\nभविता भार्गवे राम इति मामब्रवीद्भृगुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I said to him, 'Brahmin, there should be an end to the curse.' Then Bhrigu said to me: 'It will come when you meet Rama of the Bhrigu line.'"}},{"n":23,"text":"सोऽहमेतां गतिं प्राप्तो यथा नकुशलं तथा ।\nत्वया साधो समागम्य विमुक्तः पापयोनितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I came to this state, which is no good one, but meeting you, good man, I am freed from a sinful birth.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा नमस्कृत्य ययौ रामं महासुरः ।\nरामः कर्णं तु सक्रोधमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this and bowed, the great asura went away. Then Rama spoke these words to Karna in anger."}},{"n":25,"text":"अतिदुःखमिदं मूढ न जातु ब्राह्मणः सहेत् ।\nक्षत्रियस्यैव ते धैर्यं कामया सत्यमुच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fool, this is a grief no brahmin could ever bear. Such endurance is that of a kshatriya alone. Tell me the truth, as you wish.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"तमुवाच ततः कर्णः शापभीतः प्रसादयन् ।\nब्रह्मक्षत्रान्तरे सूतं जातं मां विद्धि भार्गव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, afraid of a curse and seeking to placate him, said: \"Know me, Bhargava, as one born between brahmin and kshatriya, a charioteer."}},{"n":27,"text":"राधेयः कर्ण इति मां प्रवदन्ति जना भुवि ।\nप्रसादं कुरु मे ब्रह्मन्नस्त्रलुब्धस्य भार्गव ॥","meaning":{"en":"People on earth call me Karna, Radha's son. Be gracious to me, brahmin, for I was greedy for weapons."}},{"n":28,"text":"पिता गुरुर्न संदेहो वेदविद्याप्रदः प्रभुः ।\nअतो भार्गव इत्युक्तं मया गोत्रं तवान्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no doubt that a father is a teacher, a lord who gives knowledge of the Vedas; so I named my lineage before you as Bhargava.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"तमुवाच भृगुश्रेष्ठः सरोषः प्रहसन्निव ।\nभूमौ निपतितं दीनं वेपमानं कृताञ्जलिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of the Bhrigus, angry and yet seeming to smile, said to Karna, who had fallen on the ground, wretched, trembling, with joined palms."}},{"n":30,"text":"यस्मान्मिथ्योपचरितो अस्त्रलोभादिह त्वया ।\nतस्मादेतद्धि ते मूढ ब्रह्मास्त्रं प्रतिभास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because you served me with a lie here, out of greed for weapons, therefore, fool, this Brahma weapon will not come to your mind when you need it."}},{"n":31,"text":"अन्यत्र वधकालात्ते सदृशेन समेयुषः ।\nअब्राह्मणे न हि ब्रह्म ध्रुवं तिष्ठेत्कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"It will fail except at the hour of your death, when you meet a man equal to yourself. For the Brahma weapon can never stay firmly with a non-brahmin."}},{"n":32,"text":"गच्छेदानीं न ते स्थानमनृतस्येह विद्यते ।\nन त्वया सदृशो युद्धे भविता क्षत्रियो भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go now. There is no place here for one who lies. There will be no kshatriya on earth equal to you in battle.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु रामेण न्यायेनोपजगाम सः ।\nदुर्योधनमुपागम्य कृतास्त्रोऽस्मीति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by Rama, he left in due order, and having gone to Duryodhana he said, \"I have completed my weapons training.\""}}]}]}